   $q$Which sentence would best conclude the draft if added after sentence 10?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kowalczyk writes that the sensor box sends its readings by radio every second or two.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Everyone should learn how to read weather maps so they can make their own forecasts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Weather balloons are usually made of a thin, stretchy material that grows as the balloon climbs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Kowalczyk's details show that balloons help forecasters by reaching high air and sending readings fast enough for early warnings.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kowalczyk's details show that balloons help forecasters by reaching high air and sending readings fast enough for early warnings.$q$, $q$The choice about reaching high air and sending readings fast connects both paragraphs, reaching high air and sending readings fast, back to the claim in sentence 2. The choice about the radio readings only repeats sentence 7 without explaining the whole draft.$q$, 'draft', 'f4d5d3d9-ad53-55b1-a094-6a30d5e02f64')
