insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9d881e6d-8728-5251-b1f6-5e61a5904fe4', 'wg6-writing-with-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Changing Colors of the Octopus$q$, $q$(1) Kenji Watanabe's article "The Octopus Disappears" explains how and why octopuses can change the color and pattern of their skin so quickly. (2) Watanabe shows that an octopus changes color mainly to hide and to send messages. (3) He explains that the octopus's skin holds thousands of tiny sacs of color that it can open or squeeze shut in less than a second. (4) ____. (5) This detail shows that hiding is one of the main reasons for the color change.

(6) Color change also helps octopuses communicate. (7) Watanabe writes that an octopus may suddenly flash dark stripes across its body when another octopus comes too close to its den. (8) Octopuses have eight arms. (9) He adds that the other octopus usually turns and swims away soon after seeing the dark stripes appear. (10) ____, the stripes seem to work like a warning sign.$q$, 'draft')
