        '6-8', $q$Draft: The Walking School Bus$q$, $q$(1) In the article "All Aboard on Foot," Nadia Haddad describes a walking school bus, in which a group of children walks to school together with adult volunteers. (2) ____. (3) Haddad reports that in one town, the number of students who walked to school went from twelve to sixty in a single year. (4) Parents told her they felt safer because an adult always walked at the front and the back of the group. (5) This shows that the program made walking feel safe enough for families to try.

