        '6-8', $q$No More Late Fees$q$, $q$(1) Every year, many children in Harlow stop borrowing books because they owe money to the public library. (2) The Harlow Public Library should stop charging fines for overdue books. (3) Late fees are supposed to teach responsibility, but they often punish families who simply cannot pay. (4) When a student owes even a few dollars, the library blocks that student's card until the fee is paid. (5) The library also has a nice reading corner with beanbag chairs.

(6) Some people believe that without fines, borrowers will keep books forever. (7) This worry makes sense, because the library needs its books returned. (8) ______ a nearby town that ended fines two years ago found that most overdue books still came back within a month. (9) Its librarians also reported that three hundred former members returned and opened new cards.

(10) Libraries exist so that everyone can read and learn. (11) Fines are dumb and nobody likes them.$q$, 'draft')
