  ('e5ab7054-b998-5225-9067-5ad4df08b15f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Sentence (11) is too informal for an argument. Which revision best keeps a formal style and follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ending late fees would welcome readers back while the books still come home.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The library should also stay open later on weekends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Fines are really unfair, and honestly they are kind of pointless.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Some fines may be fair, so the library could keep them for now.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ending late fees would welcome readers back while the books still come home.$q$, $q$The correct revision is formal and sums up both the benefit and the answer to the opposing worry. The choice about keeping some fines gives up the writer's own claim.$q$, 'draft', '11f9d7ea-4513-559b-92ea-4207ed898ebb')
