  ('55d31939-e367-5d3f-b507-03616e858f47', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (9) that explains how the evidence answers the opposing claim. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This proves that no library anywhere has ever lost a book after it ended fines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"The nearby town also built a new playground next to its library that same year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Some borrowers in that town still kept their books for longer than a month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weakens-claim"},{"text":"These results suggest that removing fines brings readers back without causing the library to lose its books.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$These results suggest that removing fines brings readers back without causing the library to lose its books.$q$, $q$The correct sentence explains what the evidence in sentences (8) and (9) means for the worry about lost books. The choice claiming no library ever lost a book overstates what one town's results can prove.$q$, 'draft', '11f9d7ea-4513-559b-92ea-4207ed898ebb')
