  ('aa7f3d47-2af0-5a11-8a44-8040680460d8', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (5) that explains why this evidence supports the claim. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the stickers stop the reflections that fool birds, they address the cause of the collisions at our school.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some birds that hit windows are able to fly away after resting for a few minutes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weakens-claim"},{"text":"Stickers are the only way that anyone has ever protected birds from glass.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Dot stickers come in many colors and shapes, such as stars, circles, and squares.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the stickers stop the reflections that fool birds, they address the cause of the collisions at our school.$q$, $q$The correct sentence connects the evidence in sentences (3) and (5) to the claim by showing the stickers fix the real cause. The sentence about birds flying away actually weakens the argument instead of explaining it.$q$, 'draft', 'c42445ce-0a05-5ad9-ac2d-0786dfeff77e')
