  ('11cd4e48-2d1e-5cf7-b691-93da010c8ac4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Sentence (2) is informal and unclear. Which revision states the claim most clearly and formally?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The depot is a very old building on Front Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-claim"},{"text":"Some people like the depot, and other people like parking lots.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-position"},{"text":"I kind of think the depot is pretty cool and should maybe stay.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Millbrook should turn the old depot into a history museum instead of tearing it down.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Millbrook should turn the old depot into a history museum instead of tearing it down.$q$, $q$The correct revision takes a precise, formal position that the reasons in sentences (3) through (5) support. The choice "I kind of think the depot is pretty cool and should maybe stay" keeps the casual, uncertain wording of the original.$q$, 'draft', 'a403329d-ccee-58fc-b1b7-63d03a6a0a78')
