  ('5edd1afc-806e-5aa9-85b3-84f74ed66f3c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank as sentence (8)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Parking lots are ugly, and no sensible person should want one downtown.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Parking is a real concern, but a new lot is not the only answer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Therefore, the depot should probably be torn down after all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-claim"},{"text":"Many shoppers also enjoy visiting the bakery on Front Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Parking is a real concern, but a new lot is not the only answer.$q$, $q$The correct sentence admits the opposing point has merit and then leads into the writer's response in sentences (9) and (10). The choice calling parking lots ugly insults the other side instead of answering it.$q$, 'draft', 'a403329d-ccee-58fc-b1b7-63d03a6a0a78')
