  ('66b69eea-9b19-5bca-a7b7-8a85683a1f82', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (12) so that the conclusion follows from the whole argument. Which sentence is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The council should also repave Front Street sometime next summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"History is important, and everyone should care about it more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"By opening a museum and guiding drivers to Mill Road, the council can protect this landmark and still help shoppers.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Parking lots are needed in every town, so the council's plan has some value.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weakens-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By opening a museum and guiding drivers to Mill Road, the council can protect this landmark and still help shoppers.$q$, $q$The correct sentence ties together both parts of the argument: the museum plan and the answer to the parking concern. The sentence about history is true but too general to sum up this specific argument.$q$, 'draft', 'a403329d-ccee-58fc-b1b7-63d03a6a0a78')
