  ('970706c0-1893-5a26-82b2-cbaf6e89d588', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which piece of evidence would best support sentence (6)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many adults use laptops every day at their jobs in offices and stores.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"The district technician drives a blue van from one school to the next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"At Pine Hill, three former help desk volunteers went on to join the high school's computer science program.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Each laptop at Lakeside weighs about three pounds and comes with a charging cord.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$At Pine Hill, three former help desk volunteers went on to join the high school's computer science program.$q$, $q$Sentence (6) says the desk builds skills that lead toward technology careers, and the Pine Hill volunteers show that path. The fact that adults use laptops does not show that help desk students learn anything.$q$, 'draft', '7ae270f9-354d-5e65-a996-1c19e1be7c85')
