        '6-8', $q$Play First, Then Eat$q$, $q$(1) At Birchwood Middle School, students eat lunch first and then go outside for recess. (2) Many students rush through their food so they can get outside sooner, and full trays often end up in the trash. (3) Birchwood should switch the schedule so that recess comes before lunch. (4) When students play first, they arrive at lunch hungry and calm instead of eager to leave. (5) A school in a nearby district tried this change and measured how much food was thrown away. (6) After one month, food waste dropped by about one third. (7) Teachers there also said students were more settled in afternoon classes.

(8) Opponents say that students would be too sweaty or tired to eat after playing. (9) ______ students could wash their hands and get water before entering the cafeteria, which would give them a few minutes to cool down. (10) Recess at our school is usually around twenty minutes long.

(11) Changing the order of recess and lunch would cost the school nothing.$q$, 'draft')
