   $q$Read the sentence: "When the curtain rose the nervous excited actors stepped onto the small wooden stage." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"When the curtain rose the nervous, excited actors stepped onto the small wooden stage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-introductory-comma"},{"text":"When the curtain rose, the nervous, excited actors stepped onto the small, wooden stage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-cumulative-adjectives"},{"text":"When the curtain rose, the nervous, excited actors stepped onto the small wooden stage.","is_correct":true},{"text":"When the curtain rose, the nervous excited actors stepped onto the small, wooden stage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-reversed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When the curtain rose, the nervous, excited actors stepped onto the small wooden stage.$q$, $q$A comma follows the introductory clause, and "nervous" and "excited" are coordinate adjectives that take a comma. "Wooden stage" is a unit, so adding a comma after "small" is the tempting but incorrect extra comma.$q$, 'draft', null)
