   $q$Which sentence about the team celebration is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The team celebrated loudly after the final whistle blew.","is_correct":true},{"text":"After the final whistle blew the team celebrated loudly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-introductory-comma"},{"text":"The team celebrated loudly, after the final whistle blew.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-ending-dependent-clause"},{"text":"After the final whistle, blew the team celebrated loudly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The team celebrated loudly after the final whistle blew.$q$, $q$When a dependent clause like "after the final whistle blew" comes after the main clause, it usually needs no comma. The version that opens with the "After" clause is missing the comma that should follow it.$q$, 'draft', null)
