   $q$Read the sentence: "Mount Arbel which is the tallest peak in the park was covered in snow by October." Which revision is punctuated and capitalized correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mount Arbel which is the tallest peak in the park, was covered in snow by October.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"Mount Arbel, which is the tallest Peak in the Park, was covered in snow by October.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"common-noun-capitalized"},{"text":"mount Arbel, which is the tallest peak in the park, was covered in snow by October.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"proper-noun-lowercase"},{"text":"Mount Arbel, which is the tallest peak in the park, was covered in snow by October.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mount Arbel, which is the tallest peak in the park, was covered in snow by October.$q$, $q$The name already identifies the mountain, so the "which" clause is extra information set off by commas on both sides, and "Mount Arbel" is capitalized as a proper name. "Peak" and "park" are common nouns here, so capitalizing them is incorrect.$q$, 'draft', null)
