  ('06c5392b-72fa-59c9-bdfa-cc272ec97ca4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The writer wants to add dialogue after sentence 6 to show that Tomas is frustrated. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tomas told me that he was frustrated with how our oven was working.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-dialogue"},{"text":"\"Your chocolate looks great,\" Tomas called to another group happily.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-focus"},{"text":"\"Everyone else's chocolate is melting,\" he muttered. \"Ours isn't even warm.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"This is the best science project ever,\" Tomas said with a grin.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dialogue-off-mood"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Everyone else's chocolate is melting," he muttered. "Ours isn't even warm."$q$, $q$The correct choice uses Tomas's own words to compare their oven with the others, which shows his frustration. The choice "Tomas told me that he was frustrated" only reports his feeling, so it is a summary rather than dialogue.$q$, 'draft', 'ea2b8934-ab36-5302-9e7e-5f661c696ea4')
