   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 16 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Solar ovens can be built from many different kinds of boxes and materials.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"After that, we threw the box away and walked back inside for lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"},{"text":"Tomas and I built an oven from a pizza box, some foil, and plastic wrap.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"},{"text":"Our oven melted the chocolate last, but we were the only pair who learned to follow the sun.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Our oven melted the chocolate last, but we were the only pair who learned to follow the sun.$q$, $q$The correct choice gives the result and shows what the narrator learned from turning the box, which ties back to sentences 9 through 13. The choice about walking inside ends the story without any reflection.$q$, 'draft', 'ea2b8934-ab36-5302-9e7e-5f661c696ea4')
