-- Passage wg7-narrative-writing-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d1d1d39c-d039-54a2-a4e7-525c97637e8f', 'wg7-narrative-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$A Room Full of Wires$q$, $q$(1) For our history project, each student had to interview an older relative about a job from the past. (2) I chose my grandmother, Nana Rose, because she always said her first job was "a room full of wires." (3) On Saturday afternoon, I sat across from her at the kitchen table with my notebook open. (4) She pulled out a black-and-white photograph of a long row of women wearing headsets. (5) "That was the telephone exchange in 1964," she said. (6) "Every call in town came through our hands." (7) She explained that operators connected callers by plugging cords into a giant board full of holes. (8) I had always pictured phones working by themselves, so I could hardly imagine it. (9) My cousin has a new phone with a bright purple case.

(10) Nana Rose said the busiest night was the evening of a huge snowstorm, when hundreds of families called to check on each other. (11) She worked until midnight without a break. (12) I asked whether she had been scared of making mistakes. (13) She laughed and said her hands moved so fast that she didn't have time to be scared.

(14) I wrote down everything she said.$q$, 'draft')
