   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 best uses descriptive detail to show the busy night?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She worked until midnight, which is the time when one day turns into the next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundant-fact"},{"text":"She worked very, very hard that night until it was extremely late.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-intensifiers"},{"text":"The snowstorm that night dropped almost a foot of snow on the whole town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"shifts-focus"},{"text":"She plugged in cord after cord until midnight while tiny lights blinked all over the board.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She plugged in cord after cord until midnight while tiny lights blinked all over the board.$q$, $q$The correct choice adds sights and actions from the switchboard, so the reader can picture the busy night. The choice with "very, very hard" only adds vague words instead of details.$q$, 'draft', 'd1d1d39c-d039-54a2-a4e7-525c97637e8f')
