-- Passage wg7-narrative-writing-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1d816e2f-5f4b-570d-b66a-a482a9cfbf42', 'wg7-narrative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Thirty Cents$q$, $q$(1) Every spring, the Maple Hill library holds a used book sale to raise money for new shelves. (2) This year, Mr. Haddad, the librarian, put me in charge of the children's table. (3) I arranged the picture books by color so the table looked like a rainbow. (4) The doors opened at nine, and a crowd of families poured in. (5) A small boy in a green raincoat walked straight to my table and picked up a thick book about sharks. (6) He studied the price sticker for a long time. (7) Then he opened his fist and counted three coins onto the table.

(8) The book cost one dollar, and he had only thirty cents. (9) Sharks have lived in the ocean for millions of years. (10) I didn't know what to do, because I wasn't supposed to change any prices. (11) I asked Mr. Haddad, and he told me to use my judgment. (12) I walked back and told the boy that the shark book was on a special sale. (13) His face lit up.

(14) The sale raised four hundred dollars, and I went home.$q$, 'draft')
