values
  ('3c99b413-a9d6-5122-98ca-1e615e98ab48', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 14 as a conclusion that reflects on what the experience meant?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In the end, I learned that rules should be broken whenever you feel like it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-lesson"},{"text":"We raised four hundred dollars that day, but the number I remember most is thirty cents.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The library uses the money from the sale to buy new shelves every single year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"The boy left with his shark book, and I sold many more books after he left.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$We raised four hundred dollars that day, but the number I remember most is thirty cents.$q$, $q$The correct choice gives the result and shows that the moment with the boy mattered most, echoing the title. The choice about breaking rules is tempting, but the narrator asked permission first, so that lesson does not fit the story.$q$, 'draft', '1d816e2f-5f4b-570d-b66a-a482a9cfbf42')
