values ('d2fee9da-b752-5f2a-aa2b-ca660101fb4f', 'wg7-narrative-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-narrative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Wrong Stop$q$, $q$(1) Last October, I rode the city bus by myself for the first time. (2) My plan was simple: take the Number 12 bus to Pine Street and walk one block to my grandfather's apartment. (3) I sat by the window and watched the stores slide past. (4) I was so busy reading a comic book that I forgot to count the stops. (5) When I finally looked up, nothing outside looked familiar. (6) My heart started to pound. (7) Comic books often have bright colors and speech bubbles.

(8) I made myself take three slow breaths. (9) Then I remembered what my dad had told me that morning: if you get lost, ask the driver. (10) I walked to the front of the bus and spoke to the driver. (11) She told me to stay on, because the bus would loop back to Pine Street in ten minutes. (12) I sat right behind her. (13) I watched every street sign carefully until Pine Street appeared.

(14) I got to my grandfather's apartment.$q$, 'draft')
