insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f0d6b995-c185-53ae-b591-6120de1a9939', 'wg7-paragraph-transitions-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-paragraph-transitions'), null,
        '6-8', $q$A Sport Without Referees$q$, $q$(1) Ultimate is a team sport played with a flying disc on a long field. (2) Two teams of seven players try to score by catching the disc in the opposing end zone. (3) A player who catches the disc must stop running and pass it within ten seconds. (4) ____, if a pass is dropped or knocked down, the other team takes over. (5) What makes ultimate truly unusual, though, is the way games are judged.

(6) In most youth ultimate games, there are no referees on the field. (7) Instead, players make their own calls about fouls and about whether a catch was in bounds. (8) When two players disagree, they talk it over calmly and decide how to restart play. (9) This idea is called the "spirit of the game," and teams even give each other spirit scores after a match. (10) Our school's track team practices on the field next to ours. (11) For me, learning to settle arguments fairly has been just as valuable as learning to throw a perfect pass.$q$, 'draft')
