values
  ('9a6e12c0-234d-56f4-a219-a2889897a3e4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-paragraph-transitions'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to add a topic sentence before sentence 1. Which sentence would introduce the first paragraph best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Snow can make roads slippery and close schools for the day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic"},{"text":"Water vapor is the gas form of water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Weather is one of the most interesting topics in all of science.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"A snowflake's delicate shape forms step by step as it falls.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A snowflake's delicate shape forms step by step as it falls.$q$, $q$The first paragraph describes, in order, how a speck becomes a crystal with lacy arms, so a sentence about the shape forming step by step introduces it. The sentence about weather is too broad because the paragraph is only about how snowflakes form.$q$, 'draft', 'b29390a6-cef7-55b0-b93f-e32aff1127e5')
