   $q$Read the sentence: "Dmitri watered the tomato plants they had wilted in the heat." What is wrong with it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a comma splice because a comma joins two clauses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-comma-splice"},{"text":"It is a fragment because it has no subject.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-fragment"},{"text":"It is a run-on because two independent clauses run together with no punctuation.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Nothing is wrong; it is a correct compound sentence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-run-on"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a run-on because two independent clauses run together with no punctuation.$q$, $q$"Dmitri watered the tomato plants" and "they had wilted in the heat" are both independent clauses, and nothing separates them, so the sentence is a run-on. There is no comma at all, so it cannot be a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
