   $q$Read the sentence: "The trail was muddy ___ we wore our old boots." Which choice correctly completes the sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"muddy, we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"muddy so, we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-comma"},{"text":"muddy we","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"muddy, so we","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$muddy, so we$q$, $q$Two independent clauses can be joined with a comma followed by a coordinating conjunction, and "so" also shows that the mud caused the choice of boots. A comma alone between the clauses would create a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
