   $q$Read the sentence: "Stay in your seats until the bell rings." Which part is the dependent clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"the bell rings","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-subordinating-word"},{"text":"in your seats","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"phrase-as-clause"},{"text":"Stay in your seats","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"independent-as-dependent"},{"text":"until the bell rings","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$until the bell rings$q$, $q$"until the bell rings" has a subject and verb but begins with the subordinating word "until," so it cannot stand alone. "the bell rings" without "until" could be its own sentence, so by itself it is not dependent.$q$, 'draft', null)
