   $q$Read the sentence: "Omar studied the map carefully, ___ he still took the wrong turn." Which word best shows the relationship between the two ideas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"so","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"cause-not-contrast"},{"text":"yet","is_correct":true},{"text":"and","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"addition-not-contrast"},{"text":"or","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"choice-not-contrast"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$yet$q$, $q$Taking a wrong turn after studying the map carefully is a surprise, so the contrast word "yet" fits. "So" would wrongly suggest that studying the map caused the wrong turn.$q$, 'draft', null)
