   $q$Read the sentences: "The bridge was closed for repairs. Drivers took the long route through town." Which combination best shows that one event caused the other?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bridge was closed for repairs, but drivers took the long route through town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-instead-of-cause"},{"text":"The bridge was closed for repairs, or drivers took the long route through town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"choice-instead-of-cause"},{"text":"Although the bridge was closed for repairs, drivers took the long route through town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concession-instead-of-cause"},{"text":"Because the bridge was closed for repairs, drivers took the long route through town.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the bridge was closed for repairs, drivers took the long route through town.$q$, $q$"Because" signals cause and effect: the closed bridge is the reason drivers went the long way. "Although" signals an unexpected contrast, which does not match these ideas.$q$, 'draft', null)
