  ('e907b3d1-1e73-57be-9ea4-651e5c791ac7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-sentence-structure'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Mateo forgot his calculator, he borrowed one from Jae." Which revision correctly fixes the error?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mateo forgot his calculator, however he borrowed one from Jae.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"conjunctive-adverb-with-comma"},{"text":"Mateo forgot his calculator he borrowed one from Jae.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"Mateo forgot his calculator, so he borrowed one from Jae.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mateo forgot his calculator, he then borrowed one from Jae.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adverb-does-not-fix-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mateo forgot his calculator, so he borrowed one from Jae.$q$, $q$Adding the coordinating conjunction "so" after the comma correctly joins the two independent clauses. Adding "then" does not help, because "then" is an adverb, not a conjunction, so the comma splice remains.$q$, 'draft', null)
