   $q$Which sentence correctly attaches a dependent clause to an independent clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ravi kept practicing his free throws until the gym lights went off.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ravi kept practicing his free throws, the gym lights went off.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"},{"text":"Until the gym lights went off Ravi, kept practicing his free throws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-subject-verb"},{"text":"Ravi kept practicing his free throws. Until the gym lights went off.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ravi kept practicing his free throws until the gym lights went off.$q$, $q$"until the gym lights went off" is a dependent clause, and when it comes at the end of the sentence it attaches directly with no comma needed. Setting it off with a period leaves it as a fragment.$q$, 'draft', null)
