   $q$Read the sentences: "Ms. Okafor teaches seventh-grade science. She keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom." Which choice combines them into a complex sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ms. Okafor, teaching seventh-grade science and keeping a pet tortoise in her classroom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"Ms. Okafor teaches seventh-grade science, and she keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compound-as-complex"},{"text":"Ms. Okafor, who teaches seventh-grade science, keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Ms. Okafor teaches seventh-grade science, she keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ms. Okafor, who teaches seventh-grade science, keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom.$q$, $q$"who teaches seventh-grade science" is a dependent relative clause inside the independent clause "Ms. Okafor keeps a pet tortoise in her classroom," so the sentence is complex. The "and" version is correct but compound, since both clauses are independent.$q$, 'draft', null)
