   $q$Read the sentence: "The volunteers who cleaned the beach collected over forty bags of trash." What type of sentence is it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"simple","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-relative-clause"},{"text":"compound-complex","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overcounts-clauses"},{"text":"complex","is_correct":true},{"text":"compound","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-as-compound"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$complex$q$, $q$"who cleaned the beach" is a dependent relative clause inside the independent clause "The volunteers collected over forty bags of trash," so the sentence is complex. It is easy to call it simple because there is no comma, but the relative clause has its own subject ("who") and verb ("cleaned").$q$, 'draft', null)
