   $q$Read the sentence: "Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons, it held twelve pounds before it finally cracked." Which revision fixes the error without changing the meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons, and it held twelve pounds before it finally cracked.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons. Holding twelve pounds before it finally cracked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons, it then held twelve pounds before it finally cracked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adverb-does-not-fix-splice"},{"text":"Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons it held twelve pounds before it finally cracked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Building the model bridge out of craft sticks took the team three full afternoons, and it held twelve pounds before it finally cracked.$q$, $q$The original is a comma splice hidden behind a long first clause; adding "and" after the comma correctly joins the two independent clauses. Inserting "then" does not fix it, because "then" is an adverb and cannot join clauses.$q$, 'draft', null)
