   $q$Read the sentences: "The library extended its hours. More students came to study after school. The librarian hired two assistants." Which combination best shows how the three ideas are related?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Although the library extended its hours, more students came to study after school, so the librarian hired two assistants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concession-instead-of-cause"},{"text":"The library extended its hours, but more students came to study after school, or the librarian hired two assistants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-conjunctions"},{"text":"The library extended its hours, more students came to study after school, and the librarian hired two assistants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-in-series"},{"text":"Because the library extended its hours, more students came to study after school, so the librarian hired two assistants.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the library extended its hours, more students came to study after school, so the librarian hired two assistants.$q$, $q$The ideas form a chain of causes: longer hours brought more students, and more students led to new assistants, so "Because" and "so" show both links. "Although" wrongly suggests that more students coming was surprising after the hours were extended.$q$, 'draft', null)
