   $q$Read the words: "Even though the science fair judges had already scored most of the projects and were packing up their clipboards near the stage." Why is this group of words a fragment?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It has no subject telling who is acting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-existing-subject"},{"text":"It has no verb telling what anyone did.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-existing-verb"},{"text":"It is a dependent clause with no independent clause to complete it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is too long to be written as a single sentence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"length-equals-run-on"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a dependent clause with no independent clause to complete it.$q$, $q$"Even though" makes everything after it a dependent clause, and no main clause follows to say what happened, so it is a fragment. It does have a subject ("judges") and verbs ("had scored," "were packing"), and length alone never makes a sentence wrong.$q$, 'draft', null)
