   $q$Read the sentences: "The weather was perfect. The hike was canceled. The guide was sick." Which combination best shows the relationships among the ideas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Although the weather was perfect, the hike was canceled because the guide was sick.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Although the guide was sick, the hike was canceled because the weather was perfect.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swaps-cause-and-contrast"},{"text":"Because the weather was perfect, the hike was canceled, although the guide was sick.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-relationships"},{"text":"The weather was perfect, the hike was canceled, the guide was sick.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-in-series"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Although the weather was perfect, the hike was canceled because the guide was sick.$q$, $q$The perfect weather is a surprising contrast to the cancellation, and the guide's illness is the cause, so "Although" goes with the weather and "because" goes with the illness. The choice that begins "Although the guide was sick" swaps these and makes good weather the reason for canceling.$q$, 'draft', null)
