  ('09564d23-b9de-578d-8496-38a0fa3d8302', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 would best conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mori's article shows that printed hands work well because families can afford new ones and children enjoy wearing them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"In the end, the printed hands are good, and the volunteers are very nice people.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-conclusion"},{"text":"In the end, every child in the world will soon have a printed plastic hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Mori writes that a regular artificial hand can cost thousands of dollars to make.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mori's article shows that printed hands work well because families can afford new ones and children enjoy wearing them.$q$, $q$The choice saying "families can afford new ones and children enjoy wearing them" sums up both paragraphs, cost and design, and links them to the claim. Saying the hands "are good" stays vague and does not explain what the evidence showed.$q$, 'draft', 'db32e9c7-e803-5ade-877f-b477ea42993f')
