   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 9 that explains the evidence. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This shows that letting children design their hands does more than make them look nice, because it helps the children actually use them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This shows that Ana is a very creative girl who likes to draw stars and planets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"This shows that a printed hand costs far less than a regular artificial hand does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-analysis"},{"text":"This shows that purple is the most popular color for children who wear printed hands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This shows that letting children design their hands does more than make them look nice, because it helps the children actually use them.$q$, $q$Sentence 9 says children who choose colors wear their hands more, so the best explanation connects design to daily use. The point about cost is true but explains paragraph 1, not the evidence in sentence 9.$q$, 'draft', 'db32e9c7-e803-5ade-877f-b477ea42993f')
