insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5a32dc42-4e7d-5d98-8542-caa08b12437e', 'wg8-argument-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Room for the Arts$q$, $q$(1) At Lakeview Middle School, eighth graders can choose between study hall and an elective in art or music. (2) Most students choose study hall because it seems easier. (3) Our school should require every eighth grader to take at least one semester of art or music. (4) Studying the arts teaches skills that matter in every subject. (5) When students learn to read sheet music, for example, they practice recognizing patterns, which is also an important skill in math. (6) Art classes ask students to plan a project, revise it after feedback, and finish it on time. (7) My favorite painter uses a lot of bright colors in her landscapes.

(8) Critics of this idea say students need study hall to keep up with homework. (9) It is true that eighth graders have a heavy workload. (10) Teachers at Lakeview report that many students spend study hall talking instead of working. (11) Also, a single semester of art or music would still leave students a full semester of study hall.

(12) The arts should not be treated as an extra. (13) They help students become better learners, and every eighth grader deserves the chance to experience them.$q$, 'draft')
