insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9aab30c1-d84c-5302-9a2f-304cbee33f5f', 'wg8-argument-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$A Coding Course for Brookside$q$, $q$(1) Computers are part of almost every job today, from farming to filmmaking. (2) Some people like computers and some people do not. (3) Brookside Middle School should offer a required coding course for all eighth graders. (4) Learning to code builds problem-solving skills. (5) When a program does not work, students must find the error, test a new idea, and try again. (6) This process is the same kind of careful thinking that scientists and engineers use. (7) Coding also prepares students for future careers. (8) A report from the state labor department predicts that jobs requiring computer skills will grow faster than most other jobs over the next ten years.

(9) Some students argue that coding is too difficult for beginners. (10) Beginner courses use simple, block-based programs that let students build games and animations without typing complicated commands. (11) Lots of kids at my old school did it and they were fine.

(12) A required coding course would give every Brookside student skills for the classroom and beyond.$q$, 'draft')
