   $q$Read the sentence: "After the final buzzer sounded the crowd rushed onto the court." Which revision correctly uses a comma to show the pause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After the final buzzer sounded the crowd, rushed onto the court.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-between-subject-verb"},{"text":"After the final buzzer sounded, the crowd rushed onto the court.","is_correct":true},{"text":"After, the final buzzer sounded the crowd rushed onto the court.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-after-first-word"},{"text":"After the final buzzer, sounded the crowd rushed onto the court.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After the final buzzer sounded, the crowd rushed onto the court.$q$, $q$The comma belongs where the introductory clause "After the final buzzer sounded" ends and the main clause begins. Putting it after "crowd" wrongly separates the subject from its verb "rushed."$q$, 'draft', null)
