   $q$In this sentence, "however" means "in whatever way." Which version is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"However, you decide to build the model, label every part.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"however-as-transition"},{"text":"However you decide to build, the model label every part.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"},{"text":"However you decide, to build the model label every part.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splits-phrase"},{"text":"However you decide to build the model, label every part.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$However you decide to build the model, label every part.$q$, $q$When "however" means "in whatever way," it starts a clause and takes no comma after it; the comma comes at the end of the whole clause, before "label." A comma right after "However" turns it into a transition meaning "but," which does not fit.$q$, 'draft', null)
