   $q$Read the sentence: "The recipe my grandmother insists works best with fresh ginger." Which revision correctly sets off the interrupting clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The recipe my grandmother insists, works best with fresh ginger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-opening-comma"},{"text":"The recipe, my grandmother insists, works best with fresh ginger.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The recipe my grandmother insists works best, with fresh ginger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"},{"text":"The recipe, my grandmother insists works best with fresh ginger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-closing-comma"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The recipe, my grandmother insists, works best with fresh ginger.$q$, $q$"My grandmother insists" breaks into the main sentence "The recipe works best with fresh ginger," so it needs a comma on each side. Leaving out the first comma makes "the recipe my grandmother insists" read as one confusing phrase.$q$, 'draft', null)
