  ('79bcbfd4-307e-5bd1-b149-ea9a8a2cfeb4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-capitalization-punctuation'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence correctly punctuates and capitalizes the divided quotation?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"I think,\" said Paolo. \"we should test the rocket again.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"period-splits-quote"},{"text":"\"I think\" said Paolo, \"we should test the rocket again.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-comma-in-quote"},{"text":"\"I think,\" said Paolo, \"we should test the rocket again.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"I think, said Paolo, we should test the rocket again.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"speaker-tag-inside-quotes"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"I think," said Paolo, "we should test the rocket again."$q$, $q$The quotation is one sentence broken by "said Paolo," so commas set off the speaker tag, quotation marks close around each part of Paolo's words, and the second part begins with a lowercase "we." The choice with a period after "Paolo" wrongly ends the sentence and then starts a new one with a lowercase letter.$q$, 'draft', null)
